# Docker

Add or change an image only when the app is containerized. A library or a CLI with no image skips this rule.

- Base image: a pinned Python 3.12 slim tag, not `latest`.
- Run as a non-root user.
- Copy a lock or pinned requirements. Do not install test tools in the runtime image.
- `.dockerignore` excludes `.git`, `.venv`, `logs/`, secrets, and `.cursor/`.
- One process per container. The default command is the app entrypoint.

Do not add a Dockerfile as a side effect of feature work or a docs change. A pipeline change adds one only when the contract says the app is containerized.
